          "updatedAt": "2026-10-12T10:23:21Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 22,
              "body": "The dialog context holds identifiers and lifecycle state. An event, such as terminate, changes that state; the dialog context records the result, not the event. We can define the term without adding it to the dialog context:\r\n\r\n  Lifecycle Event: An action that changes the lifecycle state of a\r\n  dialog, such as establishment, modification, resumption, or\r\n  termination.",
              "createdAt": "2026-10-12T10:23:20Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-10-12T10:23:21Z"
            }
